      "side": 1,
      "message": "There should be a long comment explaining why there is a workaround for that service type so that it doesn\u0027t have its subtypes offloaded, as the commit message won\u0027t be visible when looking at the code.\n\nIt\u0027s worth pointing out that googlecast doesn\u0027t follow the DNS-SD/mDNS spec, since it has many subtypes that it replies to but doesn\u0027t announce them. If we have workarounds that should only be for services that don\u0027t follow the spec.\n\nAlso it would be good to document what the resulting behavior is: this won\u0027t hit the code path where multiple subtypes become passthrough; instead cast will only have the main type offloaded during standby, and will only reply to subtypes when hardware offload isn\u0027t running. This works also because Cast doesn\u0027t follow the intended usage of subtypes in the spec, as it always discovers for both the subtype+base type, and only uses the mDNS subtype as an optimization.",
